        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-04-10T18:53:41.520Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As a non-Playtester, I’m enjoying the various previews as well. : )</p>\n<p>I also see Omnitron learning more into the predictable-machine schtick. But then, wasn’t Omni supposed to be the <em>adaptable</em> robot A.I. that can upgrade itself for any foe (as exemplified in Adaptive Plating Subroutine), not the systematic robot that just follows a simple, unchanging program? Now, this isn’t a criticism, I know Christopher &amp; Adam know what’s best for their creations, I just don’t see the logic here. And I know that Omnitron still flipped predictable in the first two Editions, but now it’s more pronounced. <em>And</em> I realise that it still plays random cards, but still.</p>\n<p>Yeah, <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/trajector\">@Trajector</a>, Dawn being the hardest <em>definitely</em> matches my experiences. : )</p>",
        "post_number": 121,
