        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-04-17T03:44:31.763Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Haven’t read every post in this topic, but was just looking at the KS update on variants and had a question about “first appearance” heroes.</p>\n<p>These are the first time the “current” (in the Multiverse) iterations showed up in comics? Legacy in 1948 threw me off at first, because I thought I remembered it being 1940 that basically launched superhero comics in the Metaverse. Then I realized it was a “bold new Legacy”, so this is PP VIII and not “grandpa”, right?</p>\n<p>I guess if they’re going that route, we’re not going to see Vernon Carter or Henry Goodman for a while… Still hyped about the whole thing!</p>",
        "post_number": 123,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-04-17T03:44:31.763Z",
